1
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,000
(Blossom Through the Cloud)

2
00:01:35,001 --> 00:01:37,960
(Adapted from the novel on JJWXC,
"Landing on My Heart", by Qiao Yao)

3
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,920
This pose is quite ugly.

4
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:01,120
But this face...

5
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,080
is still quite handsome.

6
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:26,720
- Morning.
- Morning.

7
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:28,599
Did you sleep...

8
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:30,400
in this position all night?

9
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:31,840
The carpet in your apartment...

10
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:33,880
is quite hard to sleep on.

11
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,200
Smiling? You're even smiling?

12
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,480
Help me. Quick, help me up.

13
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:41,080
If it's hard to sleep on,
why did you do it?

14
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:43,440
Go back to your own...

15
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:45,399
massive king-sized bed.

16
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:46,920
- My... My neck is stiff.
- You're quite heavy.

17
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,080
Slowly.

18
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:49,520
My goodness.

19
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:51,480
Lean here.

20
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:54,120
Hurry up and get up.

21
00:02:54,121 --> 00:02:55,320
I'm going to get changed.

22
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,160
Where are you going?

23
00:02:58,161 --> 00:02:59,199
To the supermarket.

24
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:00,200
What for?

25
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:01,879
To buy groceries and cook.

26
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:02,880
Cook?

27
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:04,760
You know how to cook?

28
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,560
Is cooking that hard?

29
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:08,400
I can even fly a plane.

30
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:09,960
All right, hurry up and get up.

31
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:13,160
You can cook?

32
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:17,000
If I didn't have this stiff neck,

33
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:18,960
I would really look up to you.

34
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:21,520
Can you really cook?

35
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:24,120
I'm changing. Why are you coming in?

36
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:25,680
Didn't you tell me to wash up?

37
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:28,479
Go back to your place to wash up.

38
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:29,520
This is my place.

39
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:31,560
Isn't this my home too?

40
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:33,320
Get out!

41
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,480
(Episode 16: Safe Landing
at the Next Destination)

42
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:39,880
This one?

43
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,320
No.

44
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:48,520
Then what do you want to buy?

45
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,520
I don't know.

46
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:55,200
Then what do you want to cook today?

47
00:03:57,640 --> 00:03:58,640
I don't know.

48
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:02,080
What are you looking at?

49
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:04,120
Keep looking and I'll eat you up.

50
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:07,920
Eat me up?

51
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:09,640
And how exactly do you plan
to eat me, if I may ask?

52
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:11,960
Steamed?

53
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:13,720
Boiled?

54
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:15,760
Or marinated?

55
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:17,880
Deep-fried.

56
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:20,560
That's cruel.

57
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:26,920
What are you looking at?

58
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:29,600
Looking at how pretty
my girlfriend is.

59
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:32,560
Not as pretty as you.

60
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,760
Why the sudden low self-esteem?

61
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:37,000
If I didn't have low self-esteem,

62
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:38,840
I would have
a line of husbands by now.

63
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:56,960
What are you doing?
There are so many people around.

64
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:59,040
I can't win an argument with you.
I'm not even allowed to talk back.

65
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:03,800
All right.

66
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,200
I know I was wrong.

67
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:07,680
I'm sorry.
Let me tell you,

68
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,000
next time,

69
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:13,320
if you don't reply to my messages,

70
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:14,480
get drunk,
and make me wait up so late,

71
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:18,120
you'll have to reach me
via message in a bottle.

72
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Well, thank you.

73
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:26,080
That's a bit better
than last time's funeral wreath.

74
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:29,279
Do you want some milk?

75
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:30,280
No.

76
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:33,040
You should drink some
to grow taller.

77
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:34,280
Grow taller?

78
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:36,040
Me, grow taller?

79
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:02,560
Come, put it here.

80
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:04,080
This way. There.

81
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:05,520
Right.

82
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:06,960
Come on.

83
00:06:06,961 --> 00:06:08,040
All right. Let's put them together.

84
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:09,560
Okay.

85
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:24,200
- I'm off!
- Leaving just like that?

86
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:50,280
Agarwood that cannot withstand
the wear and tear of time

87
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:52,760
How can it guard the city-state
built by predecessors?

88
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:54,720
One person, one sword

89
00:06:54,721 --> 00:06:56,119
A jar of wine, one step at a time

90
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:57,240
One step away from the heavens

91
00:06:58,720 --> 00:06:59,720
Whose world is this?

92
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:01,760
With three parts sword energy,
I'll extinguish your incense

93
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:07,640
My dear "Captain" Ruan,

94
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:09,799
I've already watched this show
too many times to count.

95
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:10,800
I don't want to watch it anymore.

96
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:12,280
Let me do it. You go rest.

97
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:13,480
No way.

98
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:15,480
Go over there.

99
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,439
I told you,

100
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:19,400
the kitchen is off-limits
to you today.

101
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:21,560
Go.

102
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:24,360
It's your stage.

103
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:26,520
Strike a pose

104
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:28,040
You're still arguing?

105
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:32,440
It looks really good.

106
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:33,600
Let me try the eggs first.

107
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:39,480
How is it?

108
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:42,320
It smells great.

109
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:43,440
You've improved a lot.

110
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:46,480
Let me try this one too.

111
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:50,280
Is it good?

112
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:52,840
The look and aroma are great.

113
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:54,880
The taste is a bit lacking.

114
00:07:58,160 --> 00:07:59,160
Let me taste it.

115
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:02,400
- It's too spicy. Don't eat it.
- I made it myself!

116
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,120
What is this?

117
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:16,480
I told you not to eat it.

118
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:22,320
Let me tell you, this flavor...

119
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:23,440
is actually perfect for me.

120
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:24,760
You people who studied abroad...

121
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,199
can stomach anything, can't you?

122
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:28,080
When I was studying abroad,
I mostly ate cold meals.

123
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:30,000
So having something hot is
already pretty good.

124
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:31,320
It's nice.

125
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:34,920
Since the Spring Festival rush
is coming,

126
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:36,320
I thought...

127
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:38,280
I would make you a nice meal.

128
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:40,560
Thanks for the hard work,
"Captain" Ruan.

129
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:43,040
But before the Spring Festival rush,

130
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:44,680
you almost sent me to the afterlife.

131
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:47,480
Weren't you enjoying it just now?

132
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,280
Yes. Let me have another bite.

133
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:51,320
Stop eating it.

134
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,960
I think I have
two packs of instant noodles.

135
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,800
- I'll make you instant noodles.
- No, really.

136
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:57,280
Forget the noodles.

137
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:59,400
This food actually suits my taste.

138
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:00,960
Besides,

139
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:02,280
it's more flavorful than noodles.

140
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:03,600
What do you mean?

141
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:05,720
Are you saying
my cooking is too heavy?

142
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:07,080
I didn't say that. It wasn't me.

143
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:08,320
Why did you come in?

144
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:10,560
I told you, the kitchen is
off-limits to you today.

145
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:13,280
Aren't we already out?

146
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:14,800
No. You need to stay out.

147
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:16,840
Go out. I'll cook.

148
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:27,080
Actually, we don't have to eat.

149
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:30,760
Not eat?

150
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:32,600
Aren't you hungry?

151
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,560
Suddenly, I feel a bit hungry.

152
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:24,320
Your suspension has been lifted.

153
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:25,560
Why the long face?

154
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:29,880
I'll get going.

155
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,400
Well...

156
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:37,320
My family might visit
during the Lunar New Year.

157
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:39,320
So I want them
to stay for a few days.

158
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,280
Do you want me...

159
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:43,200
to spend the Lunar New Year
with them?

160
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:47,240
I think you should
find some time soon...

161
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:49,640
to pack up your things.

162
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:50,960
I don't want them
to get the wrong idea.

163
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:57,520
I don't seem to have much
at your place.

164
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,360
I'll get going.

165
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:37,200
A visitor always leaves a trace.

166
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:39,080
Can you really erase it all?

167
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:48,960
- Let go.
- I'll carry it.

168
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:52,319
You said you wouldn't walk me in.

169
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:53,640
Why? Give me a reason.

170
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,799
No reason.
Why are you being like this?

171
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:56,840
Are you going back on your word?

172
00:11:57,040 --> 00:11:59,080
Why are other people's relationships
so bold and open...

173
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:00,480
and so presentable?

174
00:12:01,040 --> 00:12:02,040
Am I wrong?

175
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:03,880
If I fall in love one day,

176
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:06,760
I will walk with him openly
and proudly in public.

177
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:09,679
I wouldn't want myself,

178
00:12:09,680 --> 00:12:10,799
and especially not him,

179
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:12,880
to hide in dark corners,
keeping it a secret.

180
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:15,760
All right. I'll go in now.

181
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:17,720
Go ahead.

182
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:19,160
Bye.

183
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,240
Can I at least watch you walk in?

184
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:22,800
Sure.

185
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:51,119
Today is Lunar New Year's Eve.

186
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:54,000
Since everyone will be working
at the stroke of midnight,

187
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:57,400
I'll hand out the red packets
to everyone ahead of time.

188
00:12:57,560 --> 00:12:59,280
Happy Lunar New Year, everyone.

189
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:01,600
And for the final leg,
let's have a safe landing.

190
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:04,320
Happy Lunar New Year. Safe landing.

191
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:05,680
- Here are the red packets.
- Thank you, Captain.

192
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:08,239
- Happy Lunar New Year.
- Thank you, Captain.

193
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:10,079
- Happy Lunar New Year.
- Happy Lunar New Year.

194
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,880
- Here, Xiao Ruan.
- Happy Lunar New Year.

195
00:13:12,640 --> 00:13:14,760
Okay, let's get ready for boarding.

196
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:16,680
- Okay.
- Okay.

197
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:19,720
- Red packets!
- Time to work.

198
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:21,120
- Happy Lunar New Year.
- Let's go.

199
00:13:38,040 --> 00:13:39,040
Let's go.

200
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:52,360
- Welcome aboard.
- Welcome aboard.

201
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:54,079
Please take your seats.

202
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,080
Welcome aboard.

203
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:58,560
Hello.

204
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:00,200
- I'll help you put that in the bin.
- Okay, thank you.

205
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:02,399
Hello, I need to inform you...

206
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:04,280
that you are sitting
in the emergency exit row.

207
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:24,199
Good evening, passengers.

208
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:26,280
This is your captain speaking.

209
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:29,560
Welcome aboard
Hengshi Flight 5412...

210
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:30,640
bound for Jiangcheng.

211
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,079
The estimated flight time...

212
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:33,840
is 2 hours and 10 minutes.

213
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:35,560
Our estimated cruising altitude...

214
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:36,720
is 8,400m.

215
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:38,200
According to the weather forecast,

216
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:39,680
due to weather conditions
along the route,

217
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:41,559
we expect light turbulence...

218
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:42,880
throughout the flight.

219
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:43,999
Once you are seated,

220
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,200
please keep
your seat belts fastened.

221
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:49,839
Today is Lunar New Year's Eve,

222
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:51,360
a time for family reunions.

223
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:53,400
Travelers who have
worked hard all year...

224
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:55,280
are carrying
their achievements and longing...

225
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:56,920
as they journey back home.

226
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:58,480
In the past year,

227
00:14:59,120 --> 00:15:01,160
there were regrets and closures,

228
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:03,360
gains and partings.

229
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:06,800
But nothing can stop
the journey home.

230
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,359
The warmth of your family...

231
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:10,200
will wash away the year's hardships.

232
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:13,240
It is my honor to serve
as the captain of this flight...

233
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:14,760
and take you home for the holidays.

234
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:17,760
On behalf of the entire crew,

235
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:19,200
I wish you and your family...

236
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:20,679
a Happy Spring Festival.

237
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:21,760
In the coming year,

238
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:23,479
may you always have hope...

239
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:24,480
and be free from worries.

240
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:26,480
Follow the light
and walk in its glow.

241
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:27,920
Keep your passion alive...

242
00:15:27,921 --> 00:15:29,400
as you head
toward your next destination.

243
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:35,800
Captain, Happy Lunar New Year.

244
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:37,279
Happy Lunar New Year.

245
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:38,360
- Happy Lunar New Year.
- Happy Lunar New Year.

246
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:10,079
(Lunar New Year's Eve dinner!
The taste of home.)

247
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:11,199
(Even as an adult, I'm moved
by the Lunar New Year fireworks.)

248
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:12,360
(Happiness is simple. Fireworks
and family give my heart peace.)

249
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:16,919
(The same table, the same people.
It's the greatest blessing of all.)

250
00:16:16,920 --> 00:16:17,920
(Yue Yang)

251
00:16:17,921 --> 00:16:19,960
(The sweet burden of being pressured
by my parents to get married.)

252
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:42,800
(Mom)

253
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:46,680
Hi, Mom.

254
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:48,160
Happy Lunar New Year.

255
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:50,440
Same to you.

256
00:16:52,240 --> 00:16:53,720
You didn't come home
for the holidays.

257
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:57,520
Don't forget to send your nephew
a red packet later.

258
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:02,680
I know.

259
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:50,280
- Let's go home.
- Let's go home.

260
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:22,720
You're up.

261
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:25,200
You'll have to wait a little longer.
Don't be in a rush.

262
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:28,640
Sit down and watch some TV.

263
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:36,680
Sorry to keep you waiting.

264
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:40,480
The food is ready.

265
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:44,359
The Lunar New Year's Eve dinner is
a bit different this year.

266
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:45,640
We're having
home-cooked specialties.

267
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:47,680
What do you think?
Are you satisfied?

268
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:49,360
I am.

269
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:52,920
Here.

270
00:18:54,040 --> 00:18:55,040
As per tradition,

271
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:56,760
let's invite...

272
00:18:57,080 --> 00:18:58,240
the future Captain Ruan...

273
00:18:58,520 --> 00:18:59,600
to say a few words.

274
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:03,880
Go on.

275
00:19:04,400 --> 00:19:05,400
This is...

276
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:08,240
my first reunion dinner...

277
00:19:11,720 --> 00:19:12,960
since my father passed away.

278
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:27,880
Happy Lunar New Year.

279
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:39,360
Happy Lunar New Year.

280
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:50,880
Have a taste first.

281
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:06,880
It's delicious.

282
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:10,520
It's not bad.

283
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:18,880
She...

284
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:21,840
What's this actress's name again?

285
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:23,160
She's been very popular lately.

286
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:24,360
She's called...

287
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:27,079
Li...

288
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:28,920
- Li Zhi Huai.
- Right, Li Zhi Huai!

289
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:30,240
She's incredibly famous this year.

290
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:31,960
A few days ago, I even
watched one of her dramas.

291
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:33,760
Even you know her?

292
00:20:34,680 --> 00:20:35,680
She must be really famous then.

293
00:20:38,080 --> 00:20:39,280
Have a big dumpling.

294
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:42,680
Wait.

295
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:44,360
Before we eat the dumplings,

296
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:48,040
let's have another toast.

297
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:53,440
Ms. Ruan,

298
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:55,480
Happy Lunar New Year.

299
00:20:57,200 --> 00:20:58,200
Happy Lunar New Year.

300
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:08,160
Mr. Fu,

301
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:09,960
thank you.

302
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:22,200
(Li Zhi Huai: Ming Yu,
Happy Lunar New Year.)

303
00:21:36,320 --> 00:21:37,400
Five minutes.

304
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:40,760
You're actually timing it?

305
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:45,640
Four minutes and 30 seconds.

306
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:48,760
Why is time flying so fast?

307
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:52,880
Four minutes left.

308
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:55,880
It's gone in the blink of an eye.

309
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:58,160
I wish it would slow down.

310
00:22:02,040 --> 00:22:03,280
What happened
to your cool and aloof persona?

311
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:05,720
I can't believe you're so clingy.

312
00:22:09,120 --> 00:22:10,320
Is being clingy a bad thing?

313
00:22:13,240 --> 00:22:14,399
No,

314
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:16,119
but you can't overdo it.

315
00:22:16,120 --> 00:22:18,040
You have to leave soon.

316
00:22:19,040 --> 00:22:20,040
I don't want to leave.

317
00:22:20,600 --> 00:22:21,680
I don't want to go to work either.

318
00:22:22,960 --> 00:22:25,160
You're acting like a fatuous king.

319
00:22:25,800 --> 00:22:27,599
Don't end up labeling me...

320
00:22:27,600 --> 00:22:28,760
as a historical sinner.

321
00:22:29,760 --> 00:22:30,760
To be honest,

322
00:22:30,761 --> 00:22:32,120
you're starting to annoy me.

323
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:35,520
You're annoyed with me?

324
00:22:36,080 --> 00:22:37,560
It's only been a few days.

325
00:22:39,080 --> 00:22:40,240
Do you not like me anymore?

326
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:42,839
Didn't you say
that if I stopped liking you,

327
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:44,440
I should tell you directly,
and you would change?

328
00:22:44,880 --> 00:22:46,560
But how can I change liking you?

329
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:51,160
How can
a dignified vice president...

330
00:22:51,960 --> 00:22:53,600
act like this at home?

331
00:22:54,520 --> 00:22:56,560
Fine. Hugs and cuddles.

332
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:01,200
That's enough. Time's up.

333
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:03,199
Hurry up and go to work.

334
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:04,239
Hengshi needs you.

335
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:06,639
I'm still waiting for you
to pay my salary. Go.

336
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:08,040
You were counting down
those five minutes.

337
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:12,600
Why did you sit back down?

338
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:14,760
The routine isn't finished.

339
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:22,800
Off to work.

340
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:24,880
Now I feel refreshed.

341
00:23:25,480 --> 00:23:26,480
I'm off.

342
00:23:28,160 --> 00:23:29,160
Bye.

343
00:23:32,760 --> 00:23:33,760
He's finally gone.

344
00:23:35,920 --> 00:23:36,920
I'm exhausted.

345
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:41,679
Oh, my gosh.

346
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:42,680
He's not back again, is he?

347
00:23:46,960 --> 00:23:48,960
Xuan? Why are you here?

348
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:50,800
I missed you.

349
00:23:50,801 --> 00:23:52,760
My mom asked me
to bring you some local specialties.

350
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:55,760
Do you know
how hard it was for me...

351
00:23:56,840 --> 00:23:58,960
to bring these two boxes
of specialties?

352
00:23:59,840 --> 00:24:00,840
What's this?

353
00:24:02,120 --> 00:24:03,120
Isn't this...

354
00:24:03,640 --> 00:24:04,640
Mr. Fu's phone?
Why is it here?

355
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:08,320
It really is.

356
00:24:09,720 --> 00:24:10,720
I'll give him a call.

357
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:12,480
Sure, go ahead.

358
00:24:12,880 --> 00:24:14,680
I'll just listen to the ringtone.

359
00:24:15,480 --> 00:24:16,520
I'll call Bai Yang.

360
00:24:21,080 --> 00:24:22,080
Hello?

361
00:24:22,081 --> 00:24:24,000
Baby, did I leave my phone at home?

362
00:24:24,960 --> 00:24:25,960
Yes.

363
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:27,200
It's on the sofa.

364
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:28,760
Okay, I'll head back now to get it.

365
00:24:29,680 --> 00:24:30,680
No.

366
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:31,880
I'm about to head out anyway.

367
00:24:32,360 --> 00:24:33,560
I'll bring it to you in a bit.

368
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:35,280
Hurry to the office. Don't be late.

369
00:24:35,760 --> 00:24:36,760
Okay. Thanks for the trouble.

370
00:24:40,760 --> 00:24:41,760
I'm exhausted.

371
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:45,240
Did you drive?
I did.

372
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:48,080
I'm driving Xiao Zhen's car.

373
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:51,239
Ever since she crashed Mr. Fu's car,

374
00:24:51,240 --> 00:24:52,279
she hasn't dared to drive again.

375
00:24:52,280 --> 00:24:53,720
So this car has basically become...

376
00:24:54,280 --> 00:24:55,320
my private car.

377
00:24:58,760 --> 00:24:59,760
What?

378
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:02,199
So do you happen to not know...

379
00:25:02,200 --> 00:25:03,960
Mr. Fu's phone passcode?

380
00:25:05,840 --> 00:25:07,440
What's the point of knowing
his phone passcode?

381
00:25:08,080 --> 00:25:10,200
I would rather know
his bank card PIN.

382
00:25:10,600 --> 00:25:11,600
True.

383
00:25:11,800 --> 00:25:12,919
Good point.

384
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:14,160
Anyway, I'm going to get changed.

385
00:25:16,480 --> 00:25:17,480
The phone.

386
00:25:23,920 --> 00:25:26,000
Why don't you answer it?
It might be something urgent.

387
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:34,640
Hello?

388
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:39,520
Who is this?

389
00:25:41,720 --> 00:25:42,760
I'm looking for Fu Ming Yu.

390
00:25:43,760 --> 00:25:44,760
Is he not there?

391
00:25:46,640 --> 00:25:49,040
He left his phone with me.

392
00:25:49,440 --> 00:25:51,199
If it's urgent,

393
00:25:51,200 --> 00:25:52,800
I'll have him call you back later.

394
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:57,960
It's not urgent. I just wanted
to call and thank him.

395
00:25:58,480 --> 00:25:59,640
The flowers he sent are beautiful.

396
00:26:17,560 --> 00:26:18,600
What's wrong? What are you thinking?

397
00:26:19,680 --> 00:26:20,920
That call just now...

398
00:26:21,640 --> 00:26:22,680
was from a woman.

399
00:26:23,880 --> 00:26:25,400
So what if it was a woman?
Isn't that normal?

400
00:26:25,720 --> 00:26:26,960
Don't tell me you're jealous
over something so trivial.

401
00:26:27,560 --> 00:26:28,560
She said,

402
00:26:29,160 --> 00:26:31,960
"Thank Fu Ming Yu
for the beautiful flowers."

403
00:26:43,720 --> 00:26:45,200
Actually, I don't think
it's a big deal.

404
00:26:45,520 --> 00:26:47,239
Sending flowers is common nowadays.

405
00:26:47,240 --> 00:26:50,239
Maybe it's for a client
or a business partner.

406
00:26:50,240 --> 00:26:51,240
Don't worry about it.

407
00:26:51,241 --> 00:26:52,320
Don't worry about it?

408
00:26:53,520 --> 00:26:54,560
Then why are you speeding up?

409
00:26:55,440 --> 00:26:57,320
I really do think
sending flowers is nothing.

410
00:26:58,320 --> 00:26:59,480
It's probably just a formality.

411
00:26:59,840 --> 00:27:01,720
But that woman's approach
is quite interesting.

412
00:27:02,080 --> 00:27:03,479
She heard you answer the phone.

413
00:27:03,480 --> 00:27:05,040
Anyone with half a brain
would know...

414
00:27:05,120 --> 00:27:06,120
it was the girlfriend who answered.

415
00:27:06,520 --> 00:27:07,880
Yet, she still made a point
to tell you this.

416
00:27:08,240 --> 00:27:09,360
Since she has his number,

417
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:10,800
couldn't she just call back later?

418
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:13,280
That makes sense.

419
00:27:14,880 --> 00:27:16,120
Of course you would see through it.

420
00:27:17,520 --> 00:27:18,719
You...

421
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:20,280
really need to keep an eye out
for this woman.

422
00:27:20,840 --> 00:27:22,120
I can't be bothered to keep tabs
on so many people.

423
00:27:23,480 --> 00:27:24,720
If a man is a scumbag,

424
00:27:25,080 --> 00:27:26,680
he's like sand you can't hold onto.

425
00:27:27,200 --> 00:27:29,200
If he wants to stray,
you can't stop him.

426
00:27:30,120 --> 00:27:31,160
I can only manage myself.

427
00:27:45,760 --> 00:27:46,760
Morning, Xiao Ruan.

428
00:27:47,560 --> 00:27:48,920
A woman called just now.

429
00:27:49,080 --> 00:27:50,119
She said...

430
00:27:50,120 --> 00:27:51,880
the flowers Mr. Fu sent
were beautiful.

431
00:27:53,200 --> 00:27:54,760
She also wants him
to message her back.

432
00:27:57,960 --> 00:27:58,960
This...

433
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:02,720
Why do I sense some hostility here?

434
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:08,280
"I answered a call."

435
00:28:08,800 --> 00:28:09,839
"The woman on the other end..."

436
00:28:09,840 --> 00:28:12,040
"said the flowers he sent
were beautiful."

437
00:28:12,480 --> 00:28:13,559
"Then she reminded Fu Ming Yu..."

438
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:15,480
"to message her back
when he has time."

439
00:28:17,680 --> 00:28:18,760
Is that exactly what she said?

440
00:28:19,240 --> 00:28:20,240
That's all she said.

441
00:28:22,360 --> 00:28:23,360
Was she jealous?

442
00:28:24,640 --> 00:28:25,880
Let me mimic her for you again.

443
00:28:27,040 --> 00:28:28,320
"I answered a call."

444
00:28:28,560 --> 00:28:29,719
"The woman on the other end
said the flowers he sent..."

445
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:31,200
Okay, that's enough.
Let's leave it at that.

446
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:35,039
Mr. Fu,

447
00:28:35,040 --> 00:28:36,200
may I ask you something?

448
00:28:37,760 --> 00:28:38,760
Have you ever sent...

449
00:28:39,200 --> 00:28:40,200
Ms. Ruan flowers?

450
00:28:41,560 --> 00:28:42,599
No.

451
00:28:42,600 --> 00:28:43,679
She said she doesn't like them.

452
00:28:43,680 --> 00:28:44,920
That's not how it works.

453
00:28:45,240 --> 00:28:46,559
The more a woman says
she doesn't like something,

454
00:28:46,560 --> 00:28:48,120
the more she actually does.

455
00:28:48,440 --> 00:28:49,680
She can say
she doesn't like flowers,

456
00:28:49,960 --> 00:28:51,560
but you still have to send them.

457
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:56,560
We'll see after work.
Get back to work.

458
00:28:57,200 --> 00:28:58,200
Good luck, boss.

459
00:29:00,120 --> 00:29:01,120
Was I...

460
00:29:01,440 --> 00:29:02,560
sitting in this chair just now?

461
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:15,680
Do you have plans at home?

462
00:29:16,440 --> 00:29:17,440
Or are you coming to my place?

463
00:29:17,720 --> 00:29:18,960
I don't want to go anywhere.

464
00:29:19,200 --> 00:29:20,200
I don't want to go home either.

465
00:29:20,920 --> 00:29:22,960
Okay, then let's just wander around.

466
00:29:29,440 --> 00:29:30,440
Hello?

467
00:29:33,760 --> 00:29:34,760
Okay.

468
00:29:35,080 --> 00:29:36,080
I see.

469
00:29:39,360 --> 00:29:40,360
All right.

470
00:29:40,600 --> 00:29:41,680
We don't have to decide where to go.

471
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:43,439
I've been called in
for standby duty.

472
00:29:43,440 --> 00:29:44,480
I need to go back and pack.

473
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Where are you flying?

474
00:29:46,480 --> 00:29:47,480
Jinhai City.

475
00:29:48,040 --> 00:29:49,280
That's good. Clear your head a bit.

476
00:30:01,720 --> 00:30:02,760
Oh my gosh!

477
00:30:03,920 --> 00:30:04,920
What is it?

478
00:30:05,600 --> 00:30:07,200
Do you know Li Zhi Huai?

479
00:30:08,840 --> 00:30:10,280
Why does that name
sound so familiar?

480
00:30:11,360 --> 00:30:12,560
I think I've met her once or twice.

481
00:30:12,720 --> 00:30:14,440
I remember you two met.

482
00:30:15,040 --> 00:30:16,040
What did she want with you?

483
00:30:16,520 --> 00:30:19,520
Last time, she brought
a movie director and a producer.

484
00:30:19,920 --> 00:30:21,399
She said she wanted
to use me as a model...

485
00:30:21,400 --> 00:30:22,480
to make a biographical film.

486
00:30:22,800 --> 00:30:23,800
Did you agree?

487
00:30:24,240 --> 00:30:25,240
Of course not.

488
00:30:25,480 --> 00:30:26,480
What's there to film about me?

489
00:30:26,920 --> 00:30:27,920
Good thing you refused.

490
00:30:28,440 --> 00:30:29,440
Look at her.

491
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:30,960
She's such a media manipulator.

492
00:30:31,480 --> 00:30:33,479
She just announced
she's making a movie...

493
00:30:33,480 --> 00:30:34,480
based on a female pilot,

494
00:30:34,481 --> 00:30:35,600
and now she's involved in a scandal.

495
00:30:36,520 --> 00:30:38,280
The thing is, look.
Who is her rumored boyfriend?

496
00:30:39,440 --> 00:30:40,440
Fu Ming Yu?

497
00:30:46,400 --> 00:30:47,840
Hello? Are you back home?

498
00:30:49,640 --> 00:30:51,120
I'm flying
a last-minute flight today.

499
00:30:51,680 --> 00:30:52,680
What's up?

500
00:30:53,120 --> 00:30:54,640
Nothing. When are you coming back?

501
00:30:55,080 --> 00:30:56,080
Tomorrow.

502
00:30:56,480 --> 00:30:57,480
Okay.

503
00:30:57,920 --> 00:30:59,640
Let me know when you land.

504
00:31:00,280 --> 00:31:01,280
Okay.

505
00:31:12,920 --> 00:31:16,079
(Li Zhi Huai and Hengshi's VP
return home late at night.)

506
00:31:16,080 --> 00:31:17,080
Why has Ming Yu been...

507
00:31:17,440 --> 00:31:18,600
involved in so much drama lately?

508
00:31:20,040 --> 00:31:21,800
I just wonder if Ms. Ruan knows.

509
00:31:22,520 --> 00:31:23,679
Can she handle it?

510
00:31:23,680 --> 00:31:24,680
Ms. Ruan?

511
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:27,200
Ruan Si Xian.

512
00:31:27,400 --> 00:31:28,400
That female pilot.

513
00:31:29,080 --> 00:31:30,480
She's Fu Ming Yu's girlfriend.

514
00:31:31,600 --> 00:31:33,600
But who knows if she still is.

515
00:31:41,160 --> 00:31:42,240
(Jinhai City)

516
00:31:51,200 --> 00:31:53,080
Hello, miss.
This is your reserved table.

517
00:32:02,640 --> 00:32:03,720
Take a look to see
what you would like to order.

518
00:32:03,880 --> 00:32:04,880
Thank you.

519
00:32:10,440 --> 00:32:11,440
(Fu Ming Yu)

520
00:32:11,441 --> 00:32:12,600
Are you there yet?

521
00:32:14,040 --> 00:32:15,600
Oh no, I got busy and forgot.

522
00:32:16,120 --> 00:32:17,120
He's going to make a fuss again.

523
00:32:20,880 --> 00:32:22,440
Yes, I was a bit busy earlier.

524
00:32:24,800 --> 00:32:25,800
Okay.

525
00:32:27,200 --> 00:32:28,240
What's this?

526
00:32:28,800 --> 00:32:30,640
Back to factory settings?

527
00:32:37,400 --> 00:32:38,400
Why is there no follow-up?

528
00:32:39,360 --> 00:32:40,360
He didn't say anything else.

529
00:32:42,560 --> 00:32:44,400
He's so unapologetic.

530
00:32:44,560 --> 00:32:45,960
Everything should be fine, right?

531
00:32:55,040 --> 00:32:56,040
Look.

532
00:32:57,080 --> 00:32:58,080
"Yes,"

533
00:32:58,880 --> 00:33:00,560
"I was a bit busy earlier."

534
00:33:02,040 --> 00:33:03,040
Seven words.

535
00:33:04,120 --> 00:33:05,840
Look, in these short seven words,

536
00:33:06,160 --> 00:33:07,640
she used two punctuation marks.

537
00:33:08,040 --> 00:33:09,040
A comma...

538
00:33:09,480 --> 00:33:10,480
and a period.

539
00:33:13,280 --> 00:33:15,680
- So?
- There's a lot to unpack here.

540
00:33:16,560 --> 00:33:18,760
- Like what?
- Let me analyze it for you.

541
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:20,800
She landed at 4:10pm, right?

542
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:22,640
What time is it now?

543
00:33:22,641 --> 00:33:24,480
It's 6:37pm, Beijing time.

544
00:33:25,600 --> 00:33:26,600
Think about it.

545
00:33:26,601 --> 00:33:28,599
In the past 2 hours and 27 minutes,

546
00:33:28,600 --> 00:33:30,080
she said she was "a bit busy".

547
00:33:32,120 --> 00:33:33,640
- What was she busy with?
- What was she busy with?

548
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:36,840
Exactly. Once a pilot deboards,
it means they're off the clock.

549
00:33:36,920 --> 00:33:38,559
- What was she busy with?
- What was she busy with?

550
00:33:38,560 --> 00:33:40,240
- Who was she with?
- Who was she with?

551
00:33:42,360 --> 00:33:44,360
Just tell me. Who was she with?

552
00:33:44,480 --> 00:33:45,560
Stop keeping me in suspense.

553
00:33:47,120 --> 00:33:48,160
Looking at the trending searches.

554
00:33:50,800 --> 00:33:51,800
Think about it.

555
00:33:52,480 --> 00:33:53,680
In the past two hours,

556
00:33:54,080 --> 00:33:55,239
the discussion on this topic...

557
00:33:55,240 --> 00:33:57,000
has been absolutely explosive.

558
00:33:57,600 --> 00:33:58,639
She must have been online,

559
00:33:58,640 --> 00:34:00,920
getting the ins and outs
of the whole story.

560
00:34:04,880 --> 00:34:05,920
So do you mean...

561
00:34:06,600 --> 00:34:08,400
she already knows about this?

562
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:09,880
But she's deliberately
not saying anything...

563
00:34:11,480 --> 00:34:12,880
and acting very calm?

564
00:34:13,200 --> 00:34:14,400
The calmest waters...

565
00:34:15,600 --> 00:34:16,600
are the most dangerous.

566
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:23,000
No.

567
00:34:23,280 --> 00:34:24,400
I'm just going to call her.

568
00:34:24,920 --> 00:34:25,920
No.

569
00:34:25,960 --> 00:34:26,960
You absolutely cannot.

570
00:34:28,560 --> 00:34:29,560
Think about it.
You're out in the open,

571
00:34:31,160 --> 00:34:32,320
but she's in the dark.

572
00:34:33,040 --> 00:34:34,680
Do you know
how much information she has?

573
00:34:35,160 --> 00:34:36,160
Didn't you just say...

574
00:34:37,120 --> 00:34:38,120
she already knows?

575
00:34:39,640 --> 00:34:40,679
I was just...

576
00:34:40,680 --> 00:34:41,759
speculating.

577
00:34:41,760 --> 00:34:42,760
Just a guess.

578
00:34:43,680 --> 00:34:45,400
It's also possible
she knows nothing at all.

579
00:34:46,720 --> 00:34:48,120
But that possibility is very slim.

580
00:34:48,680 --> 00:34:50,720
Right? After all,
this news is so explosive.

581
00:34:50,960 --> 00:34:52,000
Then what should I do now?

582
00:34:54,520 --> 00:34:55,520
Test the waters.

583
00:34:57,760 --> 00:34:58,760
Try to fish for information.

584
00:34:59,360 --> 00:35:00,360
How do I do that?

585
00:35:01,120 --> 00:35:02,840
Didn't she just say
she was a bit busy?

586
00:35:04,080 --> 00:35:05,159
Ask her...

587
00:35:05,160 --> 00:35:06,160
what she was busy with.

588
00:35:10,640 --> 00:35:11,640
Good idea.

589
00:35:12,600 --> 00:35:13,600
"What are you doing?"

590
00:35:13,601 --> 00:35:15,120
Yes. Add a little smiley face.

591
00:35:16,160 --> 00:35:17,160
A cute little emoji.

592
00:35:17,560 --> 00:35:18,800
No, not that one. It's too serious.

593
00:35:19,320 --> 00:35:20,399
This one.

594
00:35:20,400 --> 00:35:21,400
Send this one.

595
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:23,079
The one with the blushing cheeks.

596
00:35:23,080 --> 00:35:24,280
- The blushing one.
- Women love that.

597
00:35:24,680 --> 00:35:25,680
Okay.

598
00:35:27,160 --> 00:35:28,279
I'm sending it then.

599
00:35:28,280 --> 00:35:29,280
Send it.

600
00:35:33,280 --> 00:35:34,680
"Hold on, I'm busy."

601
00:35:35,160 --> 00:35:36,240
Period.

602
00:35:41,440 --> 00:35:42,440
She sent that?

603
00:35:42,960 --> 00:35:44,240
She's in Jinhai.

604
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:46,720
What could she be busy with there?

605
00:35:52,480 --> 00:35:54,880
Do you know
who first discovered Ruan Si Xian?

606
00:35:55,440 --> 00:35:56,440
Yan An.

607
00:35:57,200 --> 00:36:00,200
But he just couldn't help
showing off.

608
00:36:01,520 --> 00:36:03,520
He showed the video to Fu Ming Yu.

609
00:36:03,880 --> 00:36:05,439
Then Fu Ming Yu went
straight to the aviation academy...

610
00:36:05,440 --> 00:36:06,559
to snatch her up.

611
00:36:06,560 --> 00:36:07,560
I'll admit,

612
00:36:08,120 --> 00:36:09,640
Fu Ming Yu's looks...

613
00:36:09,680 --> 00:36:11,480
can be quite deceiving.

614
00:36:11,760 --> 00:36:13,320
But Ms. Ruan...

615
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:16,000
has questionable taste.

616
00:36:16,600 --> 00:36:18,360
It's definitely a bit lacking.

617
00:36:21,160 --> 00:36:22,160
Ms. Ruan!

618
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:25,000
Are you eating here too?

619
00:36:27,880 --> 00:36:28,880
Ms. Ruan.

620
00:36:30,200 --> 00:36:31,200
I heard...

621
00:36:31,480 --> 00:36:33,960
this restaurant has a story.

622
00:36:34,080 --> 00:36:35,760
I just didn't expect...

623
00:36:35,920 --> 00:36:37,520
to hear my own story being told.

624
00:36:37,880 --> 00:36:38,880
Ms. Ruan,

625
00:36:38,881 --> 00:36:40,440
it's good that you're here.

626
00:36:40,960 --> 00:36:42,319
Mom, to be honest,
those things you asked me,

627
00:36:42,320 --> 00:36:43,800
I only know half the story.

628
00:36:44,080 --> 00:36:45,240
Now she's here.

629
00:36:45,520 --> 00:36:46,520
Please have a seat, Ms. Ruan.

630
00:36:46,521 --> 00:36:49,000
You can give us
the firsthand account.

631
00:36:49,800 --> 00:36:51,480
- It's not appropriate.
- It's perfectly appropriate.

632
00:36:51,680 --> 00:36:52,680
Join us.

633
00:36:55,360 --> 00:36:57,040
- My things...
- I'll go get them for you.

634
00:36:57,360 --> 00:36:58,360
Cutlery! Waiter!

635
00:36:58,680 --> 00:36:59,800
Bring her cutlery to this table.

636
00:37:00,120 --> 00:37:01,160
It's fine.

637
00:37:01,600 --> 00:37:03,320
- Please bring another glass too.
- Certainly.

638
00:37:07,600 --> 00:37:08,600
Here is your plate.

639
00:37:11,440 --> 00:37:12,440
Please enjoy your meal.

640
00:37:13,320 --> 00:37:14,320
This was your favorite...

641
00:37:14,321 --> 00:37:15,640
when you were little,
sweet and sour ribs.

642
00:37:17,120 --> 00:37:18,120
Eat more.

643
00:37:20,040 --> 00:37:21,759
Okay. Bring everything
to that table.

644
00:37:21,760 --> 00:37:23,120
- Sure. Please wait a moment.
- We're eating together.

645
00:37:24,600 --> 00:37:26,439
Don't be so formal.

646
00:37:26,440 --> 00:37:28,080
Just speak your mind.

647
00:37:29,760 --> 00:37:30,960
I haven't
introduced you yet, have I?

648
00:37:31,680 --> 00:37:34,240
Mom, this is Ruan Si Xian.

649
00:37:34,520 --> 00:37:35,520
And...

650
00:37:36,840 --> 00:37:39,479
this is my dearest mother,

651
00:37:39,480 --> 00:37:40,600
the famous painter,

652
00:37:40,960 --> 00:37:42,200
Ms. Dong Xian.

653
00:37:45,720 --> 00:37:46,760
Both of your names...

654
00:37:47,160 --> 00:37:48,200
share the character "Xian".

655
00:37:48,640 --> 00:37:50,720
This one right here.
The exact same character.

656
00:37:50,760 --> 00:37:51,760
An An,

657
00:37:51,840 --> 00:37:53,480
let "Captain" Ruan eat something.

658
00:37:56,320 --> 00:37:57,320
Right.

659
00:37:57,360 --> 00:37:58,680
These ribs are delicious.

660
00:37:59,920 --> 00:38:00,920
This is good too.

661
00:38:09,800 --> 00:38:10,800
Ms. Ruan,

662
00:38:11,520 --> 00:38:13,799
I have a small question...

663
00:38:13,800 --> 00:38:14,880
I've been wanting to ask.

664
00:38:15,160 --> 00:38:16,160
Go ahead.

665
00:38:17,160 --> 00:38:20,200
Did you come
to the beach alone to relax?

666
00:38:22,240 --> 00:38:24,720
So how are you feeling?

667
00:38:25,880 --> 00:38:26,960
I'm feeling quite good...

668
00:38:32,200 --> 00:38:33,200
It's just okay.

669
00:38:34,520 --> 00:38:35,880
Mom, what did I tell you?

670
00:38:36,200 --> 00:38:38,240
Ms. Ruan is a strong woman.

671
00:38:38,400 --> 00:38:39,920
She has
extraordinary mental fortitude.

672
00:38:41,040 --> 00:38:42,120
It's just her taste in men...

673
00:38:42,920 --> 00:38:44,160
that is a bit ordinary.

674
00:38:44,600 --> 00:38:46,120
An An, stop it.

675
00:38:46,720 --> 00:38:48,079
Let her eat in peace.

676
00:38:48,080 --> 00:38:49,440
Weren't you curious just now?

677
00:38:49,560 --> 00:38:51,559
Now that she's here,
you're too shy to ask.

678
00:38:51,560 --> 00:38:52,560
Curious about what?

679
00:38:53,360 --> 00:38:54,360
My private life?

680
00:38:59,720 --> 00:39:02,320
Ms. Ruan, you're truly a hero
in my heart.

681
00:39:03,720 --> 00:39:04,920
I mean it.

682
00:39:05,200 --> 00:39:07,000
If this happened to anyone else,

683
00:39:07,160 --> 00:39:08,320
they would've had a breakdown.

684
00:39:08,560 --> 00:39:09,600
But look at you,

685
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:11,079
eating and drinking as usual.

686
00:39:11,080 --> 00:39:12,440
You don't let it bother you at all.

687
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:13,720
Why would I have a breakdown?

688
00:39:14,760 --> 00:39:16,479
Zheng You An, what are you drinking?

689
00:39:16,480 --> 00:39:17,800
A sarcasm cocktail?

690
00:39:18,640 --> 00:39:19,999
You're so cynical today.

691
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:21,520
I'm not being cynical.

692
00:39:21,800 --> 00:39:23,480
I admire you...

693
00:39:23,960 --> 00:39:25,199
from the bottom of my heart.

694
00:39:25,200 --> 00:39:26,480
Heaven is my witness.

695
00:39:26,880 --> 00:39:28,079
After such a huge scandal,

696
00:39:28,080 --> 00:39:29,319
the news is blowing up,

697
00:39:29,320 --> 00:39:30,320
yet you're so calm.

698
00:39:31,480 --> 00:39:32,480
What happened?

699
00:39:35,920 --> 00:39:37,160
She doesn't know?

700
00:39:37,680 --> 00:39:38,680
Know what?

701
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:41,920
Mr. Fu.

702
00:39:42,560 --> 00:39:43,560
How's the situation?

703
00:39:43,561 --> 00:39:45,040
We can't suppress
the trending topic.

704
00:39:45,240 --> 00:39:46,800
After the Spring Festival, there is
no other entertainment news.

705
00:39:47,400 --> 00:39:48,920
Netizens finally latched onto this,

706
00:39:49,160 --> 00:39:50,799
and they've even dug up the fact...

707
00:39:50,800 --> 00:39:52,440
that you two went
to the same high school together.

708
00:39:52,640 --> 00:39:53,999
But the point is,
it was so long ago.

709
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:55,320
Why did it get exposed now?

710
00:40:00,720 --> 00:40:01,799
If one day,

711
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:04,040
you find someone else...

712
00:40:04,400 --> 00:40:05,400
without telling me,

713
00:40:06,120 --> 00:40:07,359
I'll...

714
00:40:07,360 --> 00:40:08,360
You'll what?

715
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:10,000
I'll send you a funeral wreath.

716
00:40:11,040 --> 00:40:13,080
And set it up right in the middle
of the memorial hall.

717
00:40:16,160 --> 00:40:17,200
No.

718
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:19,160
Before she comes back tomorrow,

719
00:40:19,520 --> 00:40:21,400
this matter must be resolved.

720
00:40:23,680 --> 00:40:25,000
This is a bit...

721
00:40:25,640 --> 00:40:26,640
hot.

722
00:40:26,960 --> 00:40:28,119
(Li Zhi Huai and Hengshi's VP
return home late at night.)

723
00:40:28,120 --> 00:40:30,120
They look so good together.

724
00:40:30,800 --> 00:40:31,880
Leave Li Zhi Huai out of this.

725
00:40:31,960 --> 00:40:33,240
Please focus on her work.

726
00:40:33,560 --> 00:40:34,880
Scandals, go away!

727
00:40:35,200 --> 00:40:36,520
Isn't she playing a female pilot?

728
00:40:36,760 --> 00:40:38,080
Then dating an airline executive...

729
00:40:38,160 --> 00:40:39,160
is only natural, right?

730
00:40:45,520 --> 00:40:46,559
This...

731
00:40:46,560 --> 00:40:48,000
Anyone with eyes
can see right through it.

732
00:40:48,880 --> 00:40:50,119
It's this woman...

733
00:40:50,120 --> 00:40:51,360
doing this for publicity.

734
00:40:51,840 --> 00:40:53,000
But to be fair,

735
00:40:53,400 --> 00:40:55,160
a wise man stays away from danger.

736
00:40:55,800 --> 00:40:56,800
In this matter,

737
00:40:56,801 --> 00:40:57,959
Fu Ming Yu didn't
handle it well either.

738
00:40:57,960 --> 00:40:58,960
He's in the wrong.

739
00:40:59,280 --> 00:41:00,280
An An,

740
00:41:00,281 --> 00:41:01,479
we don't know the whole story yet.

741
00:41:01,480 --> 00:41:02,800
Don't jump to conclusions.

742
00:41:03,200 --> 00:41:04,640
Look, we don't have enough food.

743
00:41:04,800 --> 00:41:05,800
Go and order two more dishes.

744
00:41:06,680 --> 00:41:07,799
Go on.

745
00:41:07,800 --> 00:41:10,560
Right. I happen to know
two really delicious dishes.

746
00:41:10,640 --> 00:41:11,640
I'll go add them.

747
00:41:12,600 --> 00:41:14,240
Ms. Ruan, it's my treat today.

748
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:15,680
Eat as much as you want.

749
00:41:15,880 --> 00:41:16,920
My treat.

750
00:41:27,960 --> 00:41:29,080
You must be quite pleased.

751
00:41:30,600 --> 00:41:31,840
You get to see me
make a fool of myself.

752
00:41:37,920 --> 00:41:38,920
I am very pleased.

753
00:41:39,960 --> 00:41:41,760
Because I have
two outstanding daughters.

754
00:41:43,400 --> 00:41:44,400
Today,

755
00:41:45,040 --> 00:41:46,040
it's a rare opportunity...

756
00:41:46,320 --> 00:41:47,560
for us to sit down
and have a meal together.

757
00:41:48,160 --> 00:41:49,160
I'm really happy.

758
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:54,600
As for your mood being affected
by other things,

759
00:41:55,800 --> 00:41:56,839
I'm sorry about that too.

760
00:41:56,840 --> 00:41:58,080
Didn't you want to talk to me...

761
00:41:59,080 --> 00:42:00,520
so that I could get
to know Fu Ming Yu better?

762
00:42:05,160 --> 00:42:06,280
I've thought about it since then.

763
00:42:06,920 --> 00:42:08,280
I think what I did before...

764
00:42:08,680 --> 00:42:10,200
did lack a sense of boundaries.

765
00:42:10,840 --> 00:42:12,320
You're already all grown up.

766
00:42:12,840 --> 00:42:14,040
You must have your own opinions.

767
00:42:15,080 --> 00:42:16,280
As for my opinion,

768
00:42:16,960 --> 00:42:18,000
it's really not that important.

769
00:42:18,680 --> 00:42:20,040
As long as you're happy.

770
00:42:21,280 --> 00:42:22,399
Isn't that how I am?

771
00:42:22,400 --> 00:42:23,400
You certainly are.

772
00:42:25,080 --> 00:42:26,080
When it comes to dating,

773
00:42:26,600 --> 00:42:27,600
just relax.

774
00:42:28,640 --> 00:42:30,360
I think the most important thing...

775
00:42:30,560 --> 00:42:32,080
is to enjoy the process.

776
00:42:33,040 --> 00:42:34,040
The result...

777
00:42:34,041 --> 00:42:35,240
is really not that important.

778
00:42:35,400 --> 00:42:38,160
So is that why you left Dad and me?

779
00:42:47,240 --> 00:42:48,280
Ruan Ruan.

780
00:42:50,160 --> 00:42:51,240
Actually, I've always...

781
00:42:51,720 --> 00:42:52,799
wanted to find a chance...

782
00:42:52,800 --> 00:42:54,880
to sit down properly
and talk to you about this.

783
00:42:57,280 --> 00:42:58,280
But...

784
00:43:01,320 --> 00:43:03,680
(Fu Ming Yu)

785
00:43:06,680 --> 00:43:07,680
Hello?

786
00:43:08,720 --> 00:43:09,720
Hello?

787
00:43:13,400 --> 00:43:14,920
There's something I want to clarify.

788
00:43:15,240 --> 00:43:16,240
Let's talk later.
Let's meet and talk tomorrow.

789
00:43:18,720 --> 00:43:19,720
Today,

790
00:43:20,680 --> 00:43:21,680
I want some peace and quiet.

791
00:43:24,160 --> 00:43:25,160
Okay.

792
00:43:36,560 --> 00:43:37,560
No need to analyze anymore.

793
00:43:38,320 --> 00:43:39,320
She definitely knows.

794
00:43:41,240 --> 00:43:42,240
What do you mean?

795
00:43:42,560 --> 00:43:43,720
What... What did she say?

796
00:43:45,040 --> 00:43:46,120
"Let's meet and talk tomorrow."

797
00:43:52,160 --> 00:43:57,120
(Departing Ep. 16 for Ep. 17)
